         How the list was made.  The plan is the build's own
         (plan-als-command.json, one of this release's files,
         index state pinned), and the closure is its executable's library
         dependencies, without the build tools (alex and happy); each
         Hackage package's license is the one its .cabal file declares in
         the last revision at or before the index state.  Checked against
         the binary: its strings carry 58 unit ids, 56 of them this plan's
         units named exactly, one GHC's own, and none disagreeing with
         the plan.  The other 84 units appear in no string (GHC writes its
         wired-in packages without versions, and most libraries leave no
         name behind), and are listed because the plan links them,
         whether or not any of their code survives the link.  They are
         adjunctions, ansi-terminal, ap-normalize, assoc, base-orphans,
         bifunctors, blaze-builder, blaze-html, boring, call-stack,
         case-insensitive, character-ps, clock, comonad, contravariant,
